 hours of sleep each night":["cayden",82.435,6.504],"during the teen years the body's internal clock called the circadian rhythm shifts later":["cayden",89.278,7.396],"this means many teens don't feel sleepy until eleven at night or later":["cayden",97.014,7.72],"screens make the problem worse because bright light can signal the brain to stay awake":["cayden",105.075,7.171],"without enough sleep it is harder to focus remember information and control emotions":["cayden",112.586,7.822],"experts suggest a few simple habits keep a regular bedtime put phones away an hour before bed and get sunlight in the morning":["cayden",120.748,11.377],"small changes can lead to better grades better moods and more energy":["cayden",132.464,6.295],"vernon dahmer a voice for the vote":["cayden",139.099,3.359],"vernon dahmer was a farmer and businessman in the kelly settlement community near hattiesburg mississippi":["cayden",142.798,9.163],"in the 1960s many black mississippians were kept from voting by unfair rules including a poll tax":["cayden",152.302,10.531],"dahmer a leader in the local naacp believed every citizen deserved a voice":["cayden",163.172,7.938],"he offered to help people register to vote and even to pay the poll tax for those who could not afford it":["cayden",171.45,9.462],"he often said if you don't vote you don't count":["cayden",181.252,4.105],"his work made him a target":["cayden",185.696,2.369],"in january 1966 the ku klux klan firebombed his home":["cayden",188.406,6.989],"dahmer defended his family so they could escape but he was badly burned and died from his injuries":["cayden",195.735,9.755],"his courage helped inspire change and in 1998 the klan leader who ordered the attack was finally convicted":["cayden",205.83,11.32],"today vernon dahmer is remembered as a hero who gave his life for the right to vote":["cayden",217.49,7.562],"should school start later":["cayden",225.392,1.958],"many high schools begin classes before eight in the morning but that schedule works against students":["cayden",227.691,8.906],"research shows that teenagers' bodies are wired to fall asleep later and wake up later":["cayden",236.937,8.669],"when schools in some districts moved start times later attendance improved and fewer students fell asleep in class":["cayden",245.945,10.84],"some people argue that later start times would make after school sports and jobs harder to schedule":["cayden",257.126,9.583],"that concern is real but schools can adjust practice times and work with local employers":["cayden",267.049,8.759],"the evidence is compelling when students are rested they learn more":["cayden",276.147,5.272],"school leaders should consider starting high school classes later":["cayden",281.759,5.343],"the harlem renaissance":["cayden",287.442,2.102],"in the 1920s a burst of creativity took place in harlem a neighborhood in new york city":["cayden",289.884,9.9],"it became known as the harlem renaissance a word that means rebirth":["cayden",300.124,6.683],"many black americans had moved north during the great migration searching for jobs and freedom from unfair laws in the south":["cayden",307.147,11.783],"in harlem writers musicians and artists shared their talents and celebrated black culture":["cayden",319.27,8.036],"langston hughes wrote poems about everyday life pride and hope":["cayden",327.646,6.563],"zora neale hurston collected folktales and wrote novels filled with southern voices":["cayden",334.55,7.735],"jazz musicians like duke ellington filled clubs with new and exciting sounds":["cayden",342.624,7.202],"the harlem renaissance showed the world the power of black art and ideas and its influence can still be felt today":["cayden",350.166,10.069],"mississippi morning a poem":["cayden",360.575,2.909],"the sun climbs slow above the pines":["cayden",363.824,3.358],"a golden ladder rung by rung":["cayden",367.522,2.921],"the porch boards creak their morning lines":["cayden",370.783,3.823],"a song my grandmother once sung":["cayden"